// gpu/ — optional single-precision BLAS path for nn/'s dense layers.
//
// This package exists as a seam, not as a working backend. nn/linear_forward
// is a 256 MFLOP scalar triple loop that runs at roughly 4 GFLOP/s against a
// single core's 50-100 GFLOP/s ceiling, so it leaves about 19x on the table
// before any device is involved. cuBLAS's `Sgemm` is the textbook fix and it
// has the same Float32 data layout this tree already uses.
//
// What is NOT here, and why
// ------------------------
// No `extern "c"` declaration. Three reasons, in order of how hard they are to
// work around later:
//
//   1. cuBLAS is not linked. The project manifest declares no `links`, and the
//      standard MoonBit toolchain has no CUDA. Linking directly would make
//      every build of nn/ require a GPU toolchain -- unacceptable for a
//      simulator whose CI runs `moon check` on a runner with no card.
//   2. The stub has to exist first. linalg_gpu solves this by compiling its
//      .cu with nvcc into a .so and dlopening it, keeping TCC free of any CUDA
//      dependency. That indirection is the right shape; its 937 lines are not
//      reusable here because all of them are Double (see below).
//   3. There is no single-precision source to reuse. moonbit_linalg_gpu wraps
//      Dgemm, Dgemv, Ddot, Dscal, Dtrsm, Dpotrf and cusolverDnDpotrf -- grep
//      for `cublasS` returns zero hits, and the one hand-written kernel there
//      is a Double `fill_kernel`. This tree is 9769 Float against 97 Double,
//      so a Float32 path is new code either way.
//
// The contract the implementation must honour
// -------------------------------------------
// liblinear_accel_sgemm returns 0 on success, ERR_LIB_NOT_LOADED (-1000) when
// liblinear_accel.so is absent, ERR_BAD_ARG (-2000) on a shape or size
// problem, and a cuBLAS status code otherwise. Anything other than 0 must be
// treated as "use the CPU path" -- that is the whole fallback contract, and it
// is why the sentinels are negative: cuBLAS itself only returns 0 or positive.
//
// Row-major in, row-major out. cuBLAS is column-major, so the stub does the
// swap internally (C = A*B is B^T*A^T in column-major). Callers never see it.
//
// Where it plugs in
// ----------------
// nn/linear_forward keeps its current body. A GPU path would dispatch at the
// top of that function once the parameter block is flattened: LinearParam
// holds weight as a flat row-major Array[Float] already, so no marshalling is
// needed on the way in, and the output buffer has the same shape.
//
// Adding this package must not change nn/ until liblinear_accel_sgemm
// actually exists on disk. A declaration with no implementation does not fail
// at build time -- it fails at load time, on a machine nobody is watching.
